Waste Collection & Recycling Management Portal 
Problem Statement 
Urban areas generate a significant amount of waste daily, including household, commercial, 
and industrial waste. Managing this waste efficiently is a major challenge for municipalities 
and private waste management agencies. In many cities, waste collection and recycling 
processes are still partially manual, fragmented, or poorly coordinated. 
Citizens often lack awareness or tools to properly dispose of waste, while authorities 
struggle with tracking collection activities, monitoring staff performance, and ensuring 
proper recycling practices. 
Current Challenges 
Lack of Centralized System 
Waste collection data is often maintained across different systems, leading to inefficiency, 
duplication, and data loss. 
Inefficient Waste Collection Scheduling 
Manual planning of collection routes leads to missed pickups, overlapping routes, and 
increased fuel costs. 
Limited Citizen Engagement 
Residents do not have a proper platform to report uncollected waste, request pickups, or 
track complaint status. 
Poor Monitoring of Waste Segregation 
There is minimal tracking of whether waste is properly segregated (dry, wet, recyclable), 
reducing recycling efficiency. 
Delay in Issue Resolution 
Complaints regarding missed collections or overflowing bins take time to resolve due to a 
lack of structured workflow. 
Lack of Transparency 
Citizens and administrators cannot easily track collection status, recycling rates, or 
operational performance. 
Inefficient Data Analysis 
Authorities struggle to generate insights such as waste volume trends, recycling efficiency, 
and area-wise performance. 
Security and Data Integrity Issues 
Existing systems may lack proper user authentication, making data vulnerable to 
unauthorized access. 
Need for the Proposed System 
To address these issues, there is a need for a web-based and/or mobile-based Waste 
Collection & Recycling Management Portal that: 
• Centralizes all waste-related data 
• Automates scheduling and tracking 
• Increases citizen participation 
• Improves recycling efficiency 
• Ensures transparency and accountability 
Proposed Solution 
The Waste Collection & Recycling Management Portal will be a role-based system with the 
following core users: 
Citizens 
• Register and log in 
• Request waste pickup 
• Report uncollected waste or issues 
• Track complaint/request status 
• Get awareness notifications on waste segregation 
Collection Staff 
• View assigned routes and schedules 
• Update collection status 
• Report issues (blocked roads, overfilled bins) 
• Upload proof (images, notes) 
Administrators (Municipality / Management) 
• Manage users and roles 
• Assign routes and schedules 
• Monitor real-time operations 
• Track complaints and resolutions 
• Generate analytical reports 
